Subject: [PATCH 050/110] feat(daemon): implement stuck-agent-dog auto-restart
 (#3340)

* feat(daemon): implement stuck-agent-dog auto-restart plugin

Replaces three "Detection only" stubs in checkDeaconHeartbeat with
actual kill-and-restart logic via new restartStuckDeacon method.

Behavior:
- Detects stuck Deacon (heartbeat stale >10min, no heartbeat after
  grace period, or pre-restart heartbeat after grace period)
- Kills tmux session, respawns via ensureDeaconRunning
- Verifies session came back
- Notifies Slack via gt-notify (zero token cost)
- Uses existing RestartTracker for exponential backoff and
  crash-loop prevention

Also adds notifySlack helper for best-effort Slack notifications
from the daemon (reads gt-notify from town bin/).

Also fixes merge conflict in internal/hooks/installer.go.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

* feat(daemon): add idle check gate to Boot spawning

Before spawning a Claude Boot session, the daemon now calls
gt-idle-check (a zero-token shell script). If the system is idle
(all rigs parked, no polecats, deacon alive), the daemon uses
degraded mechanical triage instead of spawning a Claude session.

This eliminates ~480 Claude sessions/day when Gas Town is inactive.
The wake sentinel file (.wake) allows gt sling/gt rig undock to
signal the daemon to resume full Claude Boot triage.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

